      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1774350562265,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reasoning by Analogy: This is the default mode. It involves solving problems based on what others have done or what already exists.\n\nLogic: \"Other companies build cars using steel frames and gasoline engines. Therefore, a car must have a steel frame and a gasoline engine.\"\n\nOutcome: You build a slightly better car, but you don’t reinvent transportation. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Reasoning by Analogy: This is the default mode. It involves solving problems based on what others have done or what already exists.\n\nLogic: \"Other companies build cars using steel frames and gasoline engines. Therefore, a car must have a steel frame and a gasoline engine.\"\n\nOutcome: You build a slightly better car, but you don’t reinvent transportation. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
